I'd just like to say that I appreciate the effort that the Dev Team
has put in to porting Nethack to the PC (and in general!).

I think too often when we find a problem with a piece of software,
we label it "crap," which might be appropriate if we plunked down
tons of $$ for it.  But here, there are people working on their own
time to provide us with (in general, damn good) software for free.
Think how rude it would be if you gave somebody a TV and they started
bitching about the reception on UHF channels.  It's a testament to the
DevTeam that hey keep doing this, despite all the complaints they have
to put up with from ungrateful users.

